# Backfills item icons the website can display but nothing else fetches:
# worn gear on personal bests, and every collection log slot.
# Triggered by droptracker-site-icons.timer — do not enable the service itself.
#
# For gear the primary mechanism is the ingest hook
# (data/submissions/pb._store_loadout -> utils.item_images), and this is the
# safety net: the hook only covers what it saw, not ids stored before it
# existed, ids whose download failed transiently, or ids missed while the icon
# directory was unwritable (which is how the gap went unnoticed the first time —
# every caller treats a missing icon as a soft failure, so nothing complained).
#
# For the collection log this IS the primary mechanism. A profile renders every
# slot the game defines, so it needs the whole catalogue's icons rather than
# what players have submitted; the catalogue changes only when the game does,
# which a daily pass tracks fine.
#
# Cheap by construction: reads personal_best_loadouts and one manifest row
# (never the drops table) and does one stat() per referenced id. With nothing
# missing it makes no network calls at all.
#
# Runs as `user` so a failure here proves the icon directory is still writable
# by the account the bots run as — which is the condition that actually broke.
#
# Manual dry run:  cd /store/droptracker/disc && venv/bin/python -m scripts.sweep_site_item_images
# Manual real run: sudo systemctl start droptracker-site-icons.service
# Watch it:        journalctl -u droptracker-site-icons.service -f

[Unit]
Description=DropTracker site item-icon sweep (PB gear + collection log catalogue)
Wants=network-online.target
After=network-online.target mariadb.service mysql.service

[Service]
Type=oneshot
User=user
WorkingDirectory=/store/droptracker/disc
EnvironmentFile=/store/droptracker/disc/.env
ExecStart=/store/droptracker/disc/venv/bin/python -m scripts.sweep_site_item_images --apply
TimeoutStartSec=30m
# Decorative cache warming; never urgent.
Nice=15
IOSchedulingClass=idle
